  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I've created Harbor Desk and done everything that didn't need you. It's now stopped because it needs your service keys.\n\n**Done:**\n- **Brief:** saved to `briefs/harbor_desk.md` with your text unchanged.\n- **App setup:** the app's settings are filled in and pass their checks. It will run on Vercel, under the workspace \"Harbor Pilots\".\n- **Branding:** \"Harbor Desk\" in #0B6E4F.\n- **Not needed:** no custom code, extra workspace, agent package or web address of its own. It will use its Vercel address.\n\n**Where it stopped:** 6 keys aren't set yet: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM`, `EXA_API_KEY` and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`. I tried to copy them from beta_app, your app that's already running, but this machine won't read saved key values back out of Vercel, so the copy failed. Nothing was copied and no temporary files were left behind. That means you'll need to set the keys yourself.\n\n**First key: your Cloudflare account ID.** The app stores its files with Cloudflare, so it needs to know which account is yours. This takes about 2 minutes.\n\n1. Open https://dash.cloudflare.com and sign in.\n2. On your account's home page, find **Account ID** and click to copy it. It's often shown at the bottom right of a domain's Overview page.\n3. On this machine, open a **separate** terminal window, not this chat, and go to the factory folder.\n4. Run this line:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n5. When it asks, paste the ID and press Enter.\n\nNothing shows on screen while you paste. The ID goes straight to the app's settings on Vercel and never ends up in this chat or the project's files.\n\nTell me when that's done and I'll walk you through the next key.\n\n**What comes after the keys:**\n- **Deploy:** I'll ask for your OK before starting it. It takes about 10 minutes.\n- **Tests:** about 30 minutes. Some of them need a 6-digit code emailed to someone who can sign in to the app, so I'll check with you before sending it.",
